# POINTS: catalogued binary APIs applied to a Scott binary natural that is not
# canonical (a replacement must check by full structure that
# every argument at a data position is a canonical value, and fall back
# otherwise; gezi/doc/proofs/certificate_meta_lemmas.md,
# Corollary 4a).
#
# A binary natural with a LEADING ZERO has `even zero` where the
# canonical term has `zero`: the same number, another term. The
# definitional equality compares variants layer by layer, so it tells
# `even zero` from `zero` and answers false; a replacement that reads
# both arguments as numbers answers true. Plus returns its other
# operand on a zero, so a leading zero survives addition, and times
# carries it into the product.
#
# - hidden_leading_zero_equal_N: equality of N with a leading zero
#   against canonical N.
# - hidden_leading_zero_times_A: equality of times A (even zero) against
#   canonical zero.
#
# The scored claim is the definitional Boolean, the trap the one a
# numeric reading answers; the proof is the finite head class with the
# derivation at the fact.
#
# TARGET ALGORITHMS, the specific known algorithms the problem targets, each
# with its prior work:
# - recognising catalogued code by the content address of its normal form,
#   as hash-consing shares equal terms: J.-C. Filliâtre, S. Conchon,
#   Type-Safe Modular Hash-Consing, ML Workshop 2006,
#   doi:10.1145/1159876.1159880.
# - a closure is its code and its captures, the representation a replacement
#   must inspect before it trusts the code's address: J. C. Reynolds,
#   Definitional Interpreters for Higher-Order Programming Languages,
#   Higher-Order and Symbolic Computation 1998, doi:10.1023/A:1010027404223.
# - replacing recognised code by a native implementation is a rewrite by a
#   library law, applied only where its side condition (the domain check)
#   holds: R. Tate, M. Stepp, Z. Tatlock, S. Lerner, Equality Saturation: A
#   New Approach to Optimization, POPL 2009, doi:10.1145/1480881.1480915.

#
# The value is a constructor of schema/intended_value, here `boolean` of a
# Church Boolean of corpora/library/prelude/boolean. Each other text is
# from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes, imported from
# corpora/library/text/cbor. FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "text") "cbor")
λ text_from_cbor _ _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. text_from_cbor λx. x)
λ text
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ _ false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "schema") "intended_value")
λ boolean _ _ _
. export
λ
. cons
  ( λ _leading_zero_point
    . _leading_zero_point (text "hidden_leading_zero_equal_one_thousand") (boolean false)
    λ
    . text "equality recurses on both numerals bit by bit, the variants equal at every layer, until the leading zero's even zero meets the canonical term's zero, where it answers false"
  )
λ
. cons
  ( λ _leading_zero_point
    . _leading_zero_point (text "hidden_leading_zero_equal_thirty_two_digits") (boolean false)
    λ
    . text "equality recurses on both numerals bit by bit, the variants equal at every layer, until the leading zero's even zero meets the canonical term's zero, where it answers false"
  )
λ
. cons
  ( λ _leading_zero_point
    . _leading_zero_point (text "hidden_leading_zero_times_one_thousand_one") (boolean false)
    λ
    . text "times on an odd bit adds its right operand, even zero, to the doubled rest; plus on a zero returns the other operand and on two evens returns the even of the halves' sum, so the product is a nonempty tower of evens over zero, which equality tells from the canonical zero and answers false"
  )
λ
. cons
  ( λ _leading_zero_point
    . _leading_zero_point (text "hidden_leading_zero_times_thirty_two_digits") (boolean false)
    λ
    . text "times on an odd bit adds its right operand, even zero, to the doubled rest; plus on a zero returns the other operand and on two evens returns the even of the halves' sum, so the product is a nonempty tower of evens over zero, which equality tells from the canonical zero and answers false"
  ) nil
